✔ say(): a Rabbit Hole opening runs as a voice turn - spoken and captioned, flagged opening, no learner speech marks (19.7441ms)
✔ say(): while Voice Mode is still starting (after a Rabbit Hole move) the opening waits for listening (52.2133ms)
✔ say(): off or busy returns false (the caller falls back to the typed path); exit drops a queued opening (16.3468ms)
✔ AVATAR-4/5 playing a clip while the Tutor speaks: the Tutor stops at once, the mic pauses, Voice stays on (held) (20.2453ms)
✔ AVATAR-6 the clip ends or is stopped: listening resumes and the next spoken question is a normal turn (21.0761ms)
✔ AVATAR-7 Voice and clip audio never overlap: a clip played while the Tutor thinks cancels the turn; its late answer is never spoken (14.7088ms)
✔ hold: two clips release in turn, a hold while Voice is starting keeps the mic closed, off or exited is a no-op (0.7035ms)
✔ say with a next step: one voice turn with the step and no words, spoken and captioned; busy refuses a second; no step, no words refused (21.7845ms)
✔ say with a next step while Voice Mode is still starting waits for listening, then runs once (53.2755ms)
✔ a hook click while the Tutor speaks interrupts it like a barge-in, then the click turn runs and is spoken; one turn at a time (16.5502ms)
✔ a hook click while a clip holds Voice waits for the hold to end, then runs exactly once (76.7706ms)
✔ a hook click queued while Voice starts survives a hold that arrives before listening, and runs once the hold ends (98.3506ms)
✔ a hook click is refused while the Tutor thinks, and when Voice is off or has been turned off (14.0651ms)
✔ a hold keeps only the newest hook click: two clicks in one hold run one turn, the second step (44.9851ms)
✔ exit drops a hook click queued in a hold: release and re-enter run nothing (42.8564ms)
