✔ a CAD call that returns a result completes its action in full (146.872ms)
✔ a CAD call whose provider answered with an error fails its action with no result (11.7775ms)
✔ a CAD call whose transport throws or times out fails its action with no result (11.494ms)
✔ a CAD call refused at admission fails its action with no result (9.1312ms)
✔ a CAD call whose reply is not a design fails its action with no result (9.3515ms)
✔ a CAD call whose design is refused by validation fails its action with no result (9.248ms)
✔ a CAD call whose cost is unknown still closes its action when it delivered a result (6.7349ms)
✔ a CAD reply that is not a design refunds the learner and keeps the provider cost (9.1328ms)
✔ a CAD design refused by validation refunds the learner and keeps the provider cost (8.4927ms)
✔ a failed CAD call is refunded once however often the refund or the call is repeated (12.1067ms)
✔ a CAD provider error, timeout, capacity refusal or admission refusal charges the learner nothing and needs no refund (45.8101ms)
✔ a CAD call that delivers an answer stays charged, including a review that rejects the model (34.0416ms)
✔ conversion and pricing: $1 = 100 credits = 1,000,000 micros; the worked example is 2.8 credits; no call rounds up to a credit (4.5681ms)
✔ image models are priced per modality, never one price per image (0.6614ms)
✔ Sonnet 5.5 cached input is $0.10 per million and Sonnet 5 keeps its own row; unconfirmed rates are flagged (1.5674ms)
✔ a settled charge records the price version, tier and billable quantities beside the attempt (137.7643ms)
✔ new signup: the full 2,500 credits at once; signing in again or linking a provider never makes a second allowance (13.7373ms)
✔ existing accounts keep this month and move to 2,500 at the next reset; nobody is cut mid-month; new accounts get 2,500 at once (8.6188ms)
✔ month and year rollover: renewal is computed from the period boundary, offline or not, with no carry-over (59.8258ms)
✔ the usage screen and server admission read the same entitlement (13.0446ms)
✔ concurrent spending: requests that each need most of the balance cannot all be admitted (39.338ms)
✔ exhaustion says Not enough AI credits and when they renew; a released reservation can be spent again (164.4898ms)
✔ small calls accumulate exactly: ten 0.3-credit calls are 3 credits, not 10 (11.7614ms)
✔ a job crossing midnight stays in the period it was admitted in, charged once (7.0563ms)
✔ refunds give the cost back once; the attempt keeps its recorded cost; a duplicate refund changes nothing (6.6255ms)
✔ duplicate settlement charges once; an unknown cost stays unknown (NULL, never zero) and holds nothing (7.7305ms)
✔ the cutover each environment ships: 2026-10 is the last 5,000-credit month, 2026-11 is the first 2,500 grant (21.9695ms)
✔ what each account is granted either side of the cutover: six cases, each tested; grants and usage already made are never changed (15.0734ms)
✔ the provider refuses for capacity (429, 529, 400 usage limits): the attempt settles at zero, nothing is used or held, the whole allowance can be reserved again (124.8063ms)
✔ a provider failure that is not a capacity refusal (400 invalid, 401, 403, 404, 500, 502, 503, 504, 599): the learner is charged nothing and holds nothing; the provider cost stays unknown, never zero (122.9876ms)
✔ a later settlement or refund of an unknown attempt changes nothing (settleAttempt only settles a running attempt, refundAttempt only a settled one) (55.4557ms)
✔ a transport that throws (network error, timeout, abort) is rethrown; the provider cost is unknown, the learner is charged nothing and holds nothing (25.2234ms)
✔ an answered 200 whose usage is absent or malformed is not a zero: the provider cost stays unknown, and the learner holds nothing (23.8733ms)
✔ streams: a complete stream is charged its measured cost and releases the rest; a stream that ends early or errors mid-read is an unknown provider cost, charged nothing and holding nothing (44.7268ms)
✔ the learner's reservation and the platform's spend guard are separate ledgers: releasing the learner does not release the platform's exposure for an unresolved call (62.3864ms)
✔ the October 5,000 grant and the 2,500 default: a failed call holds nothing in either month, and November starts clean (21.3671ms)
✔ duplicate settlement and refund in parallel (replay, retry, two workers) charge once and refund once, in the October 5,000 month and in November (13.7044ms)
✔ REGRESSION six HTTP 502s on PDF requests (408 credits each) hold nothing: the learner is charged nothing and the seventh request is admitted (28.8956ms)
✔ 429 reads the same on every path: a known zero and no hold (spendTransport, and ImageJobs in image-jobs.test.js); a status alone proves nothing else (13.815ms)
✔ our own admission refusal passed through a transport is not a provider error and is never recorded as a known zero (7.4191ms)
✔ a running call holds credits only within its operation's bound: held to the last second, released at the bound, then sealed once with its cost unknown (12.7997ms)
✔ each operation has its own bound: a chat call is released at 30 minutes, an image job at 4 hours, a video at 2 hours; none past 24 hours (7.3211ms)
✔ duplicate callbacks, a restart and concurrent settlement: a call sealed at its bound is released once, a late result cannot charge or settle it, and a call settled in time is charged once (7.5712ms)
✔ the bound works the same under the October 5,000 grant and the 2,500 default, and never moves a grant or a charge (6.067ms)
✔ REGRESSION a route that charged a measured call and then answered with an error refunds the learner in full, once; the provider cost stays recorded (27.3653ms)
✔ a route that answered normally keeps its charge; a failed route with nothing settled refunds nothing; free work is never refunded (10.1739ms)
