✔ repeated Retry while the cap holds and after: duplicates change nothing, no hold accumulates, each answered call settles once (221.236ms)
✔ depth drives the length target: Brief 60 to 80 s, Balanced about 90 s, Detailed up to about 2 minutes, and Gemini gets its own higher block (19.8336ms)
✔ the numbers rule is the owner's: only numbers of the card, never compute; the card-example, opening and symbol rules of v1.1 stay; the reply is a script and a separate transcript (0.8078ms)
✔ splitCard: the prose without the fences, the visuals' own words as labels, and every string and number inside a fence kept for the allowed numbers (21.2444ms)
✔ spokenNumbers reads digits and spelled-out numbers as the same values; a lone "one" is a word, not a number (3.5043ms)
✔ stripUnsafe: a sentence with a number outside the card is removed from script and transcript; the card's numbers, digits or spelled out, stay (10.1754ms)
✔ cardNumbers reads the cards own spelled-out numbers too: a card that says "four strokes" allows the script to say four (0.7866ms)
✔ stripUnsafe: a sentence the voice would say is never left in the window and the other way round (paired by position); a script symbol removes its sentence; unequal counts are cut on their own (3.7796ms)
✔ the one shared number parser reads the 40 phrases of the matcher test (and the review additions) as expected (14.2359ms)
✔ every mention carries its equivalent forms and matches the card through any of them; a fraction matches a rounded decimal; the same function reads card and script (0.9859ms)
✔ a lone zero and the counting words are free when the card has numbers; names with digits (Q1, w_0) may be said but are never the example (6.8197ms)
✔ the allowed numbers are what the learner can see: a diagram specs version, ids, node references and arrow end points are not numbers of the card (1.2338ms)
✔ counting words are not outside numbers when the card has numbers; data values still are (owner 2026-11-17; sentences from the AUD-2 real outputs) (7.673ms)
✔ a card with no numbers at all: counting words are still free (two puddles, two roles), data values are still outside (7.4904ms)
✔ one call after delivery on Gemini Flash Lite: depth, the card's prose and labels, a script and a separate transcript, the cap; the answer carries the estimate (303.3313ms)
✔ depth reaches the prompt: Detailed asks for up to about two minutes, Brief for 60 to 80 seconds; the Gemini asks are the measured higher words (106.5676ms)
✔ Gemini failing falls to Fireworks; the log carries the provider, counts and outcome, never card text (47.5442ms)
✔ an unreadable or empty answer is a failed step (the next provider runs); every step failing leaves the card alone: 200, script null, logged, nothing thrown (29.4409ms)
✔ number safety in the route: a sentence with a number outside the card is stripped from script and transcript; numbers of the card and of its diagram stay; counting words stay (12.5402ms)
✔ hard floors by depth after the strip: Brief 110, Balanced 200, Detailed 300 words, exactly; a card number must be spoken (14.1064ms)
✔ under the floor: ONE re-ask to the same model with the first answer and a user turn that names the rule; a good second answer is the script, with the counts recorded (29.7793ms)
✔ still under the floor after the one re-ask is an error answer, never short audio; there is never a second re-ask (81.4931ms)
✔ the script must speak a number of the card: none is the same re-ask, naming the rule; both rules failing is one message naming both; a card with no numbers skips the rule (75.4722ms)
✔ a card number still not spoken after the one re-ask SHIPS the script, ok, marked exampleMissing; only the floor is an error (31.8362ms)
✔ the example rule reads the numbers the prose and the question state, not a diagram: six measured cards had only a JSON version field as their number (49.9701ms)
✔ scriptInputOf is the one builder of the script input: the route, the measurement and the live check all use it; no prose numbers means no card data, whatever the diagram holds (4.6568ms)
✔ a provider failing on the re-ask hands the card to the next provider, which has no re-ask left: a short answer there is an error (12.2002ms)
✔ a step whose credential is not set is skipped; with none the call is never made; one script per card id, shared by requests in flight (46.7148ms)
✔ the script request is checked before anything is sent: method, origin, shape, size, depth; a refused caller reaches no provider (34.6783ms)
✔ first Play: ElevenLabs Flash v2.5 speaks the script (not the transcript) with the chosen voice and settings; the mp3 is kept as a file source of the owner; narration is ready (210.1211ms)
✔ a second call for the same card and script returns the kept file with no provider call; a changed script is a new file (62.2716ms)
✔ a second click while the first is generating is the same request: one provider call, one file, the same answer (71.5063ms)
✔ failure is an answer, never an exception: not configured, provider failure, refused spend, nothing stored; a retry makes the voice (44.2146ms)
✔ the voice is the learner's paid Play: no confirmation, no call; a viewer with no access cannot generate; the request is checked first (43.8177ms)
✔ the guard records usage: the voice is admitted at its characters, charged to the learner, settled; the script is recorded and never charged; both are priced rows of the registry (113.7424ms)
✔ two tabs (two isolates: a second module instance has its own in-flight map): the second Play within the window waits for the first file and is not billed; the marker is released on failure (474.2999ms)
✔ a refused admission (an exhausted allowance) is an error answer with the person's explanation, and the provider is never asked (61.8956ms)
✔ per-user rate guard: the hour cap refuses with 429 and a plain sentence; kept files and scripts are not counted (72.48ms)
✔ both routes are usage features of their own (script recorded free, voice charged) and the dev worker serves them (7.417ms)
