✔ focus: start saves learn.focus on the checkpoint and uses it as the activity focus; learn_intro tells the model the words are the focus (1283.611ms)
✔ learn_plan: the first draft is one forced tool call; the reply carries text, proposal, rows and path, nothing is written, the call is metered as learn_plan (312.3016ms)
✔ learn_plan: a provider that refuses the forced tool choice (400) is asked again with the tool on auto, and the path says so (254.0186ms)
✔ learn_plan: on auto with no tool call, one re-ask; an outline the checks refuse is re-asked once with the exact error (847.5585ms)
✔ learn_plan: a second refusal is the error response with HTTP 200 and the two rows; never a third call (603.1851ms)
✔ learn_plan: level 3 refused twice shows the valid subset when at least six ops remain, else the error response (136.9823ms)
✔ learn_plan: an edit carries the draft as a numbered list and the learner's words in a data block; rows are validated; cannot adds the nearest topic; off_plan echoes the draft (643.4554ms)
✔ learn_plan: the US$0.10 cap shrinks the file list first and refuses before any call when even the rest is over it (358.1817ms)
✔ learn_plan: a bad body is a 400 before any call; no key is a 503 (188.8427ms)
✔ learn_plan_save: the draft is saved on checkpoint.learn.plan of the active learn activity and read back with the coaching state; nothing else changes (268.1867ms)
✔ learnOf: a directory anchor stands for the files under it (shallowest first, at most 3 per directory); a missing path is still dropped (1.0178ms)
✔ a ready transcript is separate, immutable and reused by audio hash: the provider is called once (31.4964ms)
✔ failure keeps a failed record without retrying on its own; only an explicit retry calls again (3.462ms)
✔ not configured, unreadable, mismatched or silent audio yields an honest failed status and no call (3.6978ms)
✔ segments are kept only when the provider returns timing, in contract milliseconds (3.4098ms)
✔ openaiTranscriber: off unless enabled; names the real container and asks for logprobs (48.4066ms)
✔ transcription is admitted at the two-minute bound and settled at the reported token usage; a failure keeps it unknown (30.7151ms)
✔ at the daily cap transcription is refused before any call, and ensureTranscript does not record the refusal (17.0303ms)
✔ the first chunk reaches the consumer before the provider stream has finished (112.1655ms)
✔ a completed stream records timings, the request id and the allowlisted usage; never the content or the prompt (26.4193ms)
✔ a stream that ends without message_stop is unknown, a failed stream is unknown, a cancelled one is cancelled (8.9482ms)
✔ a thrown transport is logged and rethrown; a non-2xx reply is failed and returned untouched (5.2505ms)
✔ a broken telemetry database or logger never breaks the answer (16.8453ms)
✔ with TELEMETRY_DB down, a streamed answer through the real spend transport still settles its ledger rows (58.9806ms)
