✔ an explicit interactive request offers only the scene; a plain-text request never does (154.6243ms)
✔ a scene the validator refuses gets the one repair, carrying the validator's own first error (36.5058ms)
✔ a scene that still fails after its repair is no card: an honest validation error naming the scene (8.0711ms)
✔ every control setting is checked: a failure at one choice names that setting (8.4726ms)
✔ precomputed samples carry the fixed note under the content; a live scene carries none, whatever the model wrote (15.0861ms)
✔ a scene that only selects stored numbers cannot claim to calculate them live (13.4539ms)
✔ a data object with no authored size gets the size the renderer draws, so the frame never crops its cells or bars (21.7552ms)
✔ a refused spend admission is said in its own words, never as a bare status (3.422ms)
✔ L10's two wrong real scenes stay refused, each for the contradiction the review found (241.9124ms)
✔ a written calculation is checked against its own numbers; ranges, units, percentages and powers are not read (0.9642ms)
✔ a scene that passes the gates is read back by the verifier pass, setting by setting, before it becomes a card (28.0176ms)
✔ the supply-demand rerun (a false equilibrium no gate reads) is refused by the verifier pass; a corrected answer becomes the card (285.956ms)
✔ when the verifier pass cannot run, nothing is added and nothing is repaired: the reason is said (34.8733ms)
✔ the server keeps only verifier items marked false, quoted from the card, and not a number at its display precision (334.4968ms)
